.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount()
reads the open file
.I file
from its current position to the end, and stores the number of
lines, words and characters in
.IR lines ,
.I words
and
.IR chars .
A word is a group of characters separated by spaces, tabs or newlines.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success, \-1 if
.I file
is NULL.
